(`rehearsal.log`).\nPASS  separate-within-dup-shared: two equal shared forecasts within one call are not unified with each other, so C4 refuses as within one call  refused [\"('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3') base: 3 forecast nodes (v14.q3_two_a, v14.q3_two_b, v9.q3_one_v9); exactly one per scenario is required\"]\nPASS  separate-within-dup-second: the second call's two equal shared forecasts are not both unified to the first call's one (C4 refuses)  refused [\"('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3') base: 3 forecast nodes (v14.q3_one_v14, v9.q3_two_a, v9.q3_two_b); exactly one per scenario is required\"]\nPASS  abstain: an unresolved singleton is published and can be read with its card as the ground  \nPASS  verdict: a swap of two packets with identical text: INCOMPLETE (the key is not the committed one)  the key is not the one packets.md committed to\nPASS  verdict: decisions written into the key: INCOMPLETE (the key is not the committed one)  INCOMPLETE\nPASS  torn journal: recover keeps the committed entries, marks the torn attempt interrupted and the line damaged, sends nothing  single-E|single|3: interrupted\nPASS  torn journal: the interrupted card's packet says the request was started and no answer recorded  P22\nPASS  verdict: a damaged journal line makes the verdict INCOMPLETE  answers.jsonl line 72 is damaged\nPASS  joint-retry-fix: the joint pair is final-published after its retry but scored on its refused first attempt, like the separate pair  joint 6, separate 6\nPASS  separate-unit: the same number in another unit is not unified (C4 refuses)  refused\nPASS  a refused first answer whose retry was never sent is incomplete, not refused or not sent  \n61 of 61 checks pass\nCAUGHT  24 a run takes several verdicts  FAIL  verdict: a run takes one verdict; replay reproduces it from the sealed readings, and fails once they are\nCAUGHT  25 replay does not compare  FAIL  verdict: a run takes one verdict; replay reproduces it from the sealed readings, and fails once they are\nCAUGHT  26 a retry is sent before later first attempts  FAIL  every scored first attempt is sent before any retry  \nCAUGHT  27 completeness from the final attempts  FAIL  a diagnostic retry that fails in transport leaves the scored test complete  single-O|single|1: transport\nCAUGHT  28 the returned text is cut  FAIL  a long malformed answer is kept whole: the passage it names at its end is shown in the attempts file  e5\nCAUGHT  29 a null content is passed on  crash: TypeError: expected string or bytes-like object\nCAUGHT  30 a file is written before both render  FAIL  packets are written only after both files render: a failed render leaves nothing, and a second call then\n30 of 30 mutants caught; control passes\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
