{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '208,225p'; rg -n 'null content|long malformed|render leaves|after first|retry transport|during a retry|during a scored' paid_rehearsal.py rehearsal.log\"","aggregated_output":"   208\t## 3g. After council round 47f (`codex-r47f.md`)\n   209\t\n   210\t- **[47f.1] Retries cannot decide whether the scored test is complete.**\n   211\t  - The run sends every first attempt (all 36) before any retry.\n   212\t  - Completeness is judged on the first attempts: each must end published, held or refused.\n   213\t  - A retry that fails in transport, is interrupted or is never sent stays in the diagnostic record.\n   214\t  - Rehearsed: an interruption during a retry leaves all 36 scored attempts and a complete verdict. A transport failure on a retry\n   215\t    leaves the verdict complete. An interruption during a scored attempt makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. In the journal, every first\n   216\t    attempt comes before every retry.\n   217\t- **[47f.2] Every returned text survives.**\n   218\t  - The record keeps the provider's whole response, as the archive stores it, with no 20,000-character cut.\n   219\t  - A null content is shown as the model's refusal, or as \"no text returned\".\n   220\t  - Both files are rendered before anything is written, and a failed render leaves no files.\n   221\t  - Rehearsed: a refusal with null content, a 25,000-character malformed answer whose passage is named at its end, and a render that\n   222\t    fails and then succeeds.\n   223\t- **Rehearsal:** 61 of 61, three runs (`rehearsal.log`).\n   224\t- **Mutants:** 30 of 30 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`). Two mutants are caught by the crash the defence prevents:\n   225\t  - without the interrupted branch, the summary fails on an unfinished attempt;\nrehearsal.log:43:PASS  interrupt during a scored attempt: results written; that attempt interrupted, later ones not sent, no retry yet; INCOMPLETE  pair-old-1|joint|3: not sent; pair-old-1|separate-v4|3: not sent\nrehearsal.log:47:PASS  a provider refusal with null content: packets are made, and its text is in the attempts file  INCOMPLETE\nrehearsal.log:48:PASS  a long malformed answer is kept whole: the passage it names at its end is shown in the attempts file  e5404\nrehearsal.log:49:PASS  packets are written only after both files render: a failed render leaves nothing, and a second call then succeeds  \npaid_rehearsal.py:164:                raise KeyboardInterrupt('rehearsal: the launcher is stopped during a scored attempt')\npaid_rehearsal.py:185:        if s == 'long-raw' and key == ('single-E', 'single') and n == 1:   # [47f.2] a long malformed answer naming a passage at its end\npaid_rehearsal.py:459:    check('interrupt during a scored attempt: results written; that attempt interrupted, later ones not sent, no retry yet; INCOMPLETE',\npaid_rehearsal.py:478:    check('a provider refusal with null content: packets are made, and its text is in the attempts file',\npaid_rehearsal.py:484:    check('a long malformed answer is kept whole: the passage it names at its end is shown in the attempts file',\npaid_rehearsal.py:502:    check('packets are written only after both files render: a failed render leaves nothing, and a second call then succeeds',\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import contextlib, io, json\nimport paid_gate as pg, paid_rehearsal as pr\nfiles={}\nclass Mem:\n    def __init__(self, path): self.path = path\n    def __truediv__(self, name): return Mem(self.path+'\\\\''/'\\\\''+name)\n    def read_text(self, **kwargs): return files[self.path]\n    def read_bytes(self): return self.read_text().encode()\n    def write_text(self, data): files[self.path] = data\n    def exists(self): return self.path in files\nout=Mem('\\\\''run'\\\\'')\nkeys=Mem('\\\\''keys'\\\\'')\n(out/'\\\\''plan.json'\\\\'').write_text(json.dumps(pr.PLAN))\njournal=[]\nfor draw in pg.DRAWS:\n    for item in pr.PLAN:\n        base=dict(unit=item['\\\\''unit'\\\\''], arm=item['\\\\''arm'\\\\''], draw=draw, attempt=1)\n        flavour='\\\\''bad-rung'\\\\'' if (item['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],draw)==('\\\\''single-E'\\\\'',3) else '\\\\''ok'\\\\''\n        data=pr.valid_answer(item, flavour)\n        calc=pg.strip(data)\n        result=pg.cc.check(item['\\\\''family'\\\\''],item['\\\\''passages'\\\\''],calc)\n        journal.extend([dict(base,status='\\\\''started'\\\\''),dict(base,status='\\\\''answered'\\\\'',decision=pg.cc.publish_decision(item['\\\\''family'\\\\''],calc,result),data=data)])\nretry=dict(unit='\\\\''single-E'\\\\'',arm='\\\\''single'\\\\'',draw=3,attempt=2,status='\\\\''started'\\\\'')\nlines='\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\''.join(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False) for r in journal+[retry])+'\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\''\nprint('\\\\''Completed scored attempts:'\\\\'',sum(r['\\\\''status'\\\\'']=='\\\\''answered'\\\\'' for r in journal))\nfor outcome,suffix in [('\\\\''interrupted retry, no finish line'\\\\'','\\\\'''\\\\''),('\\\\''same retry, torn finish line'\\\\'','\\\\''{\\\"unit\\\":\\\"single-E\\\",\\\"arm\\\":\\\"single\\\",\\\"draw\\\":3,\\\"attempt\\\":2'\\\\''),('\\\\''scored answer includes U+2028'\\\\'','\\\\'''\\\\'')]:\n    scored_lines=lines\n    if outcome.startswith('\\\\''scored answer'\\\\''):\n        edited=[dict(r) for r in journal]\n        edited[1]['\\\\''data'\\\\'']['\\\\''answers'\\\\''][0]['\\\\''reasons'\\\\'']='\\\\''one'\\\\''+chr(0x2028)+'\\\\''two'\\\\''\n        scored_lines='\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\''.join(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False) for r in edited+[retry])+'\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\''\n    (out/'\\\\''answers.jsonl'\\\\'').write_text(scored_lines+suffix)\n    results=pg.summarise(out,pr.PLAN,None)\n    items={(i['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],i['\\\\''arm'\\\\'']):i for i in pr.PLAN}\n    order=[(f'\\\\''P{i:02}'\\\\'',list(u)) for i,u in enumerate(sorted(pg.packet_units(results,items)),1)]\n    key=dict(salt='\\\\''probe'\\\\'',run_digest=pg.run_digest(out),order=order,attempts=[])\n    (keys/'\\\\''packet-key.json'\\\\'').write_text(json.dumps(key))\n    text, rendered, _=pg.render_packets(out,key)\n    (out/'\\\\''packets.md'\\\\'').write_text(text)\n    rd={}\n    for pid, k in rendered.items():\n        rd[pid]={}\n        for token in k['\\\\''cards'\\\\'']:\n            good=k['\\\\''arm'\\\\'']\"'!='\"'\\\\''separate'\\\\'' or int(k['\\\\''draw'\\\\''])==1\n            answers={q:dict(answer='\\\\''yes'\\\\'' if good and q=='\\\\''usable'\\\\'' else '\\\\''no'\\\\'',ground=f'\\\\''{token} reading'\\\\'') for q in pg.QUESTIONS}\n            rd[pid][token]={'\\\\''A'\\\\'':answers,'\\\\''B'\\\\'':answers}\n    (out/'\\\\''readings.json'\\\\'').write_text(json.dumps(dict(packets_sha256=pg.hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),packets=rd)))\n    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()): verdict=pg.score(out,keys)\n    print(outcome, verdict['\\\\''verdict'\\\\''], (verdict['\\\\''joint usable pairs'\\\\''],verdict['\\\\''separate usable pairs'\\\\'']), verdict['\\\\''problems'\\\\''])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
