ines\n    if outcome.startswith('\\\\''scored answer'\\\\''):\n        edited=[dict(r) for r in journal]\n        edited[1]['\\\\''data'\\\\'']['\\\\''answers'\\\\''][0]['\\\\''reasons'\\\\'']='\\\\''one'\\\\''+chr(0x2028)+'\\\\''two'\\\\''\n        scored_lines='\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\''.join(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False) for r in edited+[retry])+'\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\''\n    (out/'\\\\''answers.jsonl'\\\\'').write_text(scored_lines+suffix)\n    results=pg.summarise(out,pr.PLAN,None)\n    items={(i['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],i['\\\\''arm'\\\\'']):i for i in pr.PLAN}\n    order=[(f'\\\\''P{i:02}'\\\\'',list(u)) for i,u in enumerate(sorted(pg.packet_units(results,items)),1)]\n    key=dict(salt='\\\\''probe'\\\\'',run_digest=pg.run_digest(out),order=order,attempts=[])\n    (keys/'\\\\''packet-key.json'\\\\'').write_text(json.dumps(key))\n    text, rendered, _=pg.render_packets(out,key)\n    (out/'\\\\''packets.md'\\\\'').write_text(text)\n    rd={}\n    for pid, k in rendered.items():\n        rd[pid]={}\n        for token in k['\\\\''cards'\\\\'']:\n            good=k['\\\\''arm'\\\\'']\"'!='\"'\\\\''separate'\\\\'' or int(k['\\\\''draw'\\\\''])==1\n            answers={q:dict(answer='\\\\''yes'\\\\'' if good and q=='\\\\''usable'\\\\'' else '\\\\''no'\\\\'',ground=f'\\\\''{token} reading'\\\\'') for q in pg.QUESTIONS}\n            rd[pid][token]={'\\\\''A'\\\\'':answers,'\\\\''B'\\\\'':answers}\n    (out/'\\\\''readings.json'\\\\'').write_text(json.dumps(dict(packets_sha256=pg.hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),packets=rd)))\n    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()): verdict=pg.score(out,keys)\n    print(outcome, verdict['\\\\''verdict'\\\\''], (verdict['\\\\''joint usable pairs'\\\\''],verdict['\\\\''separate usable pairs'\\\\'']), verdict['\\\\''problems'\\\\''])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"Completed scored attempts: 36\ninterrupted retry, no finish line PASS (9, 3) []\nsame retry, torn finish line INCOMPLETE (9, 3) ['answers.jsonl line 74 is damaged']\nscored answer includes U+2028 INCOMPLETE (8, 3) ['answers.jsonl line 2 is damaged', 'answers.jsonl line 3 is damaged', 'pair-old-1|joint|1: interrupted']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY**\n\nThe attempt journal can still make a completed comparison `INCOMPLETE`. In a $0 replay with all 36 scored attempts recorded, an interrupted diagnostic retry left the verdict at `PASS`. Adding only that retry’s partially written final record changed it to `INCOMPLETE`, with the same 9–3 count. A second replay showed that a valid Unicode line separator inside an answer was mistaken for a record break, causing a completed scored attempt to be reported as interrupted. [paid_gate.py:150](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:150) · [paid_gate.py:204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:204) · [paid_gate.py:698](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:698)\n\nRead records using the exact newline delimiter the writer uses, and separate scored records from diagnostic records so damage to a retry stays visible without changing the verdict. Rehearse both cases and keep the existing control where a damaged scored record makes the verdict `INCOMPLETE`."}}
